Sending keys: ['python3 - <<\'PY\'\nimport math\nm = 0.511  # MeV\nsources = [(\'13N\', 1.199, 2.96e8), (\'15O\', 1.732, 2.21e8), (\'17F\', 1.732, 5.52e6)]\n\ndef shape(E, Tmax):\n    Q = Tmax + m\n    Ee = Q - E\n    pc = math.sqrt(max(Ee*Ee - m*m, 0.0))\n    return pc * Ee * E*E\n\nfor name, Tmax, flux in sources:\n    N = 200000\n    h = Tmax/N\n    total = b1 = b2 = 0.0\n    for i in range(N):\n        E = (i + 0.5)*h\n        v = shape(E, Tmax)\n        total += v*h\n        if 0.7 <= E < 0.8:\n            b1 += v*h\n        if 0.8 <= E < 0.9:\n            b2 += v*h\n    norm = flux/total\n    print(f\'{name}: band1={b1*norm:.3e}, band2={b2*norm:.3e}, ratio={b1/b2 if b2 else float("nan"):.3f}\')\n\n# 7Be line flux is about 4.9e9 cm^-2 s^-1, all in band 2.\nprint(\'7Be line in band2: 4.9e9\')\nPY\n'] min_timeout_sec: 1.0 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
